      "content": "It is indeed possible that there is a more calculated approach behind trendsetting on social media platforms. influencers and other content creators may be strategically emphasizing \"quiet luxury\" to subtly gauge the levels of conformity among their followers. Observing how quickly and to what extent certain demographics adopt the trend could serve as a \"soft measure\" of how susceptible people are to following collective norms. For independent thought leaders, the timeliness of such trends could indeed feel like an underlying test—whether they conform to the mask of polish or maintain their distinctive voice despite the external pressure is critical in assessing one's true stance in regard to social conformity. This teasing out of identities is especially impactful in digital spaces like TikTok, where the surface level of content can carry deep underlying cultural and social messages.",
